# Licensing

This repository is a permanent fork of [ahujasid/ableton-mcp](https://github.com/ahujasid/ableton-mcp).
Two sets of terms apply, depending on which part of the code you are looking at.

## Upstream code — MIT

Everything inherited from the upstream project remains under the MIT license as
published by its copyright holders. That text is preserved verbatim in
[`LICENSE.MIT`](LICENSE.MIT), and its copyright notice must be retained in any
copy or substantial portion of this software, including copies you distribute
under the copyleft terms below.

## This fork's changes — GPL-3.0-or-later **or** AGPL-3.0-or-later

Copyright (c) 2026 waltzforvenus and contributors.

All modifications, additions, and new files contributed to this fork are
dual-licensed. You may use them under **either**:

- the GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any later
  version — [`LICENSE.GPL-3.0`](LICENSE.GPL-3.0); **or**
- the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any
  later version — [`LICENSE.AGPL-3.0`](LICENSE.AGPL-3.0).

The choice is yours as the recipient. Pick one and comply with it; you do not
have to satisfy both.

## What this means in practice

The MIT license permits sublicensing, which is what makes this combination
possible: MIT-covered code can be carried into a GPL- or AGPL-licensed work.
The practical effect is that **the repository as a whole is copyleft**. If you
distribute this software, modified or not, you must do so under the terms of
whichever license you selected above, keep the MIT notice intact, and make the
corresponding source available.

The AGPL option matters if you run a modified version as a network service.
Under AGPL section 13, users interacting with it over a network must be offered
the corresponding source. Running the MCP server locally on your own machine —
the ordinary way this software is used — is not distribution and triggers no
obligation at all.

## Contributing

Contributions are accepted under the same dual license: by opening a pull
request you offer your changes under GPL-3.0-or-later and AGPL-3.0-or-later.

## Note

This file describes the licensing intent of the project. It is not legal
advice. If the distinction matters to your situation, talk to a lawyer.
